---
description: Use agent-skills workflows from .cursor/skills
alwaysApply: true
---

Before non-trivial technical work on this project:

1. Route via `.cursor/skills/using-agent-skills/SKILL.md` (meta-skill: discovers which of the
   24 installed skills applies to the current task/phase).
2. Read and follow the matching skill under `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. Open any
   `reference.md`/`references/*.md` it links to when relevant.
3. Prefer project skills over guessing conventions; the user does not need to say "read skill"
   each time — apply this proactively.
4. This project follows `SPEC.md` at the repo root — treat it as the source of truth for scope,
   tech stack, and the mandatory crash-prevention guardrails (§6). Any skill-driven spec/plan
   artifact (e.g. output of `spec-driven-development`/`planning-and-task-breakdown`) must stay
   consistent with it, not replace it, unless the user explicitly asks to supersede it.
